course: dictionary
lesson: 9356
title: One word, many meanings: split
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Split is a word with several meanings. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «In 2026 the 48 teams were split into 12 groups of 4.» Here split means divided into parts, because the sentence talks about groups and numbers.
explain: The same word can mean something very different. «The bag split» means it tore along a line. «Split a sandwich» means share it with someone. Ask yourself: does this sentence talk about dividing, breaking, sharing, or a stretch? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: In maths, split can show a sum. «A fraction like one third means: split the whole set into equal parts and take one part.» So if you split 12 sweets into 3 equal groups, each group gets 4 sweets. In history, «The empire was split into a western half and an eastern half» means it was divided into two parts.
fact: Split can be a verb (to split) or a noun (a split).
fact: Context helps you pick the right meaning of split.
fact: «Split» can mean to divide something into parts or groups.
fact: «Split» can mean to break or tear along a line, like a bag that splits.
fact: «The splits» is a stretch with your legs straight out in a line, as in «doing the splits».
exercise: «In 2026 the 48 teams were split into 12 groups of 4.» How many teams were in each group? | 6 | 12 | *4 | 48
exercise: «A fraction like one third means: split the whole set into equal parts and take one part.» What does split mean here? | *To divide into equal parts | To shout loudly | To run away quickly | To tear along a crack
exercise: «The empire was split into a western half and an eastern half.» Find and copy the word that means divided into parts. | *split | ruled | empire | western
test: «She could do the splits in gymnastics.» What are the splits? | *A stretch with your legs straight out in a line | A crack in the wall | A loud shout | Sharing a snack with a friend
test: «The old log split along its grain.» What does split mean in this sentence? | Shared out between friends | Painted in bright colours | Counted up carefully | *Broke open along a line
exam: «Sam and Priya split the bill for the pizza.» What does split the bill mean? | *Share the cost between them | Tear the bill in half | Ask the waiter for a bigger bill | Lose the bill on the table
